# Keeps Tilt's file-watcher off the same junk .dockerignore keeps out of the
# build context (2026-07-31 investigation — see .dockerignore's header for
# the full story). Without this, Tilt was watching .otelc-build/gocache's
# 12GB Go build cache, which churns on nearly every local `go build` /
# `task otelc:generate` run — noise that can trigger rebuilds with no source
# change behind them, on top of the build-context bloat .dockerignore fixes.

.otelc-build/gocache
.otelc-build/debug
.otelc-build/debug.log
.otelc-build/build-plan.log
.otelc-build/matched.json
.otelc-build/added_imports.*.json

# otelc writes this straight into cmd/<beat>/ — the exact directory each
# beat's custom_build deps= list watches for real source changes, since
# that's where main.go lives — then removes it once the build finishes
# (.gitignore's "them per build and takes them back out"). Left unignored,
# each build's own write/remove cycle inside cmd/<beat>/ re-triggers that
# same build: an infinite loop, observed live 2026-08-11 as thump-bootstrap
# rebuilding continuously (a companion bug to the one above — that one was
# .otelc-build/ itself once listed directly in deps=, this one is a file
# inside a deps= path that's otherwise entirely legitimate to watch).
#
# The trailing "*" covers otelc.runtime.go.tmp-<random>, the temp file it
# writes before renaming into place — the bare pattern above only matched
# the final name, so the temp file's own create event was still slipping
# through and re-triggering the same loop. Confirmed live 2026-08-11 via
# `tilt get filewatch ... -o json`'s fileEvents.
cmd/*/otelc.runtime.go*

bin
dist
coverage.out
